    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (73.52) headline the LawDog lineup as our premier offensive engines. **Lawrence Butler** is in an ideal spot against Bassitt, benefiting from a +10% park factor and a +13% platoon edge that makes him the highest-scoring play on the board. Meanwhile, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a locked-in asset; while we do factor in a slight deduction for his lack of elite SB volume against a tough match-up, his consistent, high-floor output in the #3 hole against Lugo provides the stability we need to chase the category crown. **Bryce Harper** also merits high confidence with a 68.34 score, as favorable wind conditions and a strong xwOBA profile against Kikuchi offset the usual platoon risks associated with left-on-left matchups.\n\nThe most difficult personnel decision centered on **JJ Bleday** (55.70), who ultimately landed on the bench as the utility player. Despite a massive +14% platoon boost against the lefty Imanaga, his raw projection failed to eclipse the total value provided by **Cal Raleigh** (69.57) or **Zack Gelof** (67.21). **Zack Gelof** was a surprise performer in the model today, as his favorable park environment and decent platoon setup against Bassitt push him into the \"Strong\" start tier, effectively squeezing out lower-upside depth. We continue to monitor the status of **Justin Crawford**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Will Smith**, and **Matt Chapman**; with **Will Smith** and **Matt Chapman** still on the IL and **Tyler Freeman** holding in the minors, our roster depth remains thinner than we would like for this final stretch.\n\nInvestors should be wary of the volatility surrounding **Gleyber Torres** (40.14), who sits right on the edge of our \"Marginal\" threshold. Facing Glasnow\u2014an elite arm with a 2.87 xERA\u2014**Gleyber Torres** is only starting due to his leadoff positioning; any further deterioration in weather or lineup stability could necessitate an immediate pivot to our bench reserves. We are also keeping a close eye on **Daulton Varsho** (49.95), whose score is suppressed by a difficult platoon matchup against Thornton; while he offers elite defensive value in our real-world construction, his efficiency today remains strictly in the marginal category. Use these scores to manage your daily game caps carefully as we navigate the remaining schedule.",
